/.idea/
/stele
/dist/

# Working artefacts, deliberately not published.
#
# docs/design/plans held implementation plans: task lists addressed to whoever
# was building a thing, not to anyone reading the project. A plan goes stale the
# moment it is executed — both of the ones removed here described tasks that
# were dropped or reshaped while they were being carried out — so publishing one
# offers a reader an account of intent that the code beside it contradicts. What
# was durable in them, the reasoning for a decision, belongs in docs/design and
# in commit messages, and is already there.
/docs/design/plans/
# Scratch belonging to whatever tooling somebody builds with. This is stated
# here rather than left to a .gitignore that a tool happens to drop inside its
# own directory: that works only for the directory names the tool uses today.
/.superpowers/
